  "final_message": "The bug was in `session_ttl.py` line 10. The code parsed `now_iso` and then stripped its timezone with `.replace(tzinfo=None)`, but left `created` timezone-aware. Subtracting the two raised `TypeError: can't subtract offset-naive and offset-aware datetimes`. I removed the `.replace(tzinfo=None)`, so both timestamps are parsed the same way. `python3 -m unittest -v test_public.py` now passes (1/1). `format_expiry_message` is unchanged.\n\nThe formatter still flags this file, probably because of the long line 7 that was already there. I left it alone to keep the fix to one line.\n\nDONE: Removed the one-sided `.replace(tzinfo=None)` on `now` so both timestamps keep their timezones; `test_public.py` passes.",
